WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.636
Where do new pieces of DNA get

00:00:01.683 --> 00:00:02.054
added?

00:00:02.681 --> 00:00:04.039
Meet DNA polymerase.

00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:05.711
It builds the new strand.

00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:08.474
A strand has two ends, 5-prime and

00:00:08.532 --> 00:00:09.113
3-prime.

00:00:09.566 --> 00:00:11.377
Polymerase only works at one of them.

00:00:11.528 --> 00:00:13.130
Think of a train that only boards

00:00:13.165 --> 00:00:13.757
at the back.

00:00:14.291 --> 00:00:16.126
New pieces join the 3-prime end.

00:00:16.753 --> 00:00:17.124
Click.

00:00:17.658 --> 00:00:18.018
Click.

00:00:18.738 --> 00:00:19.144
Click.

00:00:19.864 --> 00:00:22.070
DNA polymerase adds new pieces only to

00:00:22.117 --> 00:00:23.057
the 3-prime end.

00:00:23.684 --> 00:00:24.949
So which way does it grow?

00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:26.156
Swipe.
